BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 457.35 Td (Caching is basically keeping a copy of data \(or a computed result\) in a faster place so future requests can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 443.95 Td (served quickly without doing the \223expensive work\224 again \(DB query, disk read, network call, heavy) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 430.55 Td (computation\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 410.65 Td (The main goal of a cache is to reduce the application latency and the load on the database.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 390.75 Td (Caching prevents repeated disk I/O, network I/O, and CPU-intensive computation, which is what makes it such a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 377.35 Td (powerful lever for scaling read traffic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 357.45 Td (Caches are super fast but also expensive and limited in size, hence we don\222t cache everything Instead, we) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 344.05 Td (strategically cache a subset of the data \(hot data\) that is most likely to be requested again.) Tj ET
