BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 778.00 Td (BENEFITS) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 758.10 Td (Highly resilient; if the cache fails, the app still functions via the DB.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 738.20 Td (Only \223hot\224 data is stored in the cache.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 718.30 Td (TRADE-OFFS) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 698.40 Td (Risk of stale data if the DB is updated without cache invalidation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 678.50 Td (BEST FOR:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 658.60 Td (High read-to-write ratios, such as e-commerce product data.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 58.00 625.70 Td (Write Through) Tj ET
q 479.00 0 0 184.15 58.00 415.95 cm /Im9 Do Q
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 406.95 Td (THE FLOW) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 387.05 Td (Every write operation is executed on both the cache and the DB at the same time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 367.15 Td (LOGIC & OWNERSHIP) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 347.25 Td (Synchronous process ensuring both layers update as one operation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 327.35 Td (BENEFITS) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 307.45 Td (Strong data consistency between cache and DB.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 287.55 Td (Future reads benefit from low latency as data is already cached.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 267.65 Td (TRADE-OFFS) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 247.75 Td (Higher write latency due to the overhead of two simultaneous writes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 227.85 Td (BEST FOR:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 207.95 Td (Consistency-critical systems like financial or transaction apps.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 58.00 175.05 Td (Write Behind / Write Back) Tj ET
