BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 272.40 Td (CPU/RAM runs out of memory, so thats when we start to think about scale.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 252.50 Td (Cache is similar to a DB, so scaling also is similar to a DB.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 232.60 Td (Vertical Scaling) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 212.70 Td (Horizontal Scaling - Either Read Replicas of cache instances\(mostly for read heavy traffic\), or Sharding the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 199.30 Td (data\(incase their are more writes in the system\). You can refer this to read about database scaling strategies) Tj ET
