BT /F2 14.5 Tf 58.00 484.02 Td (Hashing) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 458.17 Td (Hashing is a way to turn any input \(string, number, object, file\205\) into a fixed-size value called a hash \(or hash) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 444.77 Td (code\) using a hash function.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 424.87 Td (Why is it useful ?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 404.97 Td (Fast Lookup: Hash tables/maps use hashes to find items in ~O\(1\) average time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 385.07 Td (Partitioning: You can hash a key to decide which bucket/server should store it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 365.17 Td (How do you decide if a function is a good hash function ?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 345.27 Td (It should be deterministic meaning: Same input should generate the Same Hash \(always\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 325.37 Td (Uniform Distribution: Spreads the data evenly. \(to avoid hot spots\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 305.47 Td (The Modulo %N Approach) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 285.57 Td (In a distributed system, we need a way to map an incoming request \(with a key like user_id\) to one of our N) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 272.17 Td (servers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 252.27 Td (The simplest way to do this is using the Modulo operator \(%\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 232.37 Td (How it works:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 212.47 Td (We take the hash of the key: hash\("user_123"\) = 145892.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 192.57 Td (We perform modulo N \(where N is the number of servers\): 145892 % 3.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 172.67 Td (The result is the index of the server \(e.g., 0, 1, or 2\). This is great because it\222s simple, fast, and distributes keys) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 159.27 Td (fairly evenly across your servers. As long as N stays the same, everything works perfectly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 139.37 Td (Example :) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 119.47 Td (Say we have a user called \223user_123\224 and we want his request to always hit a particular database. But this) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 106.07 Td (question may arise as to why do we even need the user to hit the same server/DB ?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 86.17 Td (Because data and cache are usually partitioned, and sending the same user to different servers causes misses,) Tj ET
