BT /F2 12 Tf 58.00 499.00 Td (Proxy vs VPN) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 478.40 Td (VPN : A VPN creates a secure, encrypted tunnel for all the device's traffic \(browsers, apps, system updates\). It is) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 465.00 Td (secure because it encrypts your data, unlike proxies where it sends in plain text \(unencrypted\). \(hides IP) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 451.60 Td (system-wide\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 431.70 Td (Proxy : It only works at the application level \(e.g., just your web browser\). It doesn't usually encrypt your data; it) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 418.30 Td (just masks your IP address for that specific app. It allows only for one app not system wide. \(hides IP app-level\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 58.00 385.40 Td (Proxy vs Firewall) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 364.80 Td (Firewall : firewall sits at the edge of the network and scans incoming and outgoing data packets \(it only looks at) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 351.40 Td (the header of the data \(IP and Port\). It does not open the data. It can block/allow connections instantly based on) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 338.00 Td (rules, no need to terminate the connection\), If the data is coming from a suspicious source, the firewall stops it at) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 324.60 Td (the door before it can get into your computer. So it just filters and blocks, it does not have proxy characteristics) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 311.20 Td (like caching.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 291.30 Td (Proxy : It is a middleman that terminates the client connection and starts a new connection to the server.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 277.90 Td (Because it acts as the destination, it can "read" the data to perform caching or content filtering.) Tj ET
