BT /F2 10.5 Tf 58.00 767.00 Td (Obvious Questions that Pop-up) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 749.35 Td (What happens if all the boxes end up with 1s ?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 729.45 Td (Well, in that case the bloom filter becomes useless, because for every query it\222ll say \223maybe present\224, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 716.05 Td (we\222ll end up hitting the DB every time, this in-turn increases the false positivity rate \(which is not what we want\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 702.65 Td (so we lose the whole benefit of using it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 682.75 Td (That\222s why sizing matters: we need enough bits \(and the right number of hash functions\) so the filter doesn\222t) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 669.35 Td (get too full, and the false positive rate stays low.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 649.45 Td (So what do we do when the filter starts getting full? Can we scale it?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 629.55 Td (The common approach is to layer Bloom filters \(the idea behind scaling bloom filters\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 609.65 Td (When the current Bloom filter starts getting too full \(too many 1s -> false positives go up\), we don\222t try to expand) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 596.25 Td (the same bit array \(because we would need to rehash and reorder , not optimal\). Instead:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 576.35 Td (We freeze the current Bloom filter \(keep it as-is\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 556.45 Td (We create a new Bloom filter \(usually bigger / tuned better\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 536.55 Td (We insert all new elements into the new one) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 516.65 Td (For query\(element\) operation, you might have to check in all instances of Bloom Filters and then take a decision) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 503.25 Td (accordingly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 483.35 Td (So how do we decide the number of bits to choose, and the number of hash functions to choose ?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 463.45 Td (There\222s a lot of math involved in this one, and if you are curious to learn on how to choose the optimal k and m,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 450.05 Td (you can check these 2 wonderful articles out \(usually u just use those formulaes directly, no need to remember) Tj ET
