BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 778.00 Td (Question : We said \223producers send data to a topic\224 and \223data ends up in a partition on a broker\224 but how does) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 764.60 Td (Kafka decide which partition a record should go to? And can producers control that?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 744.70 Td (Answer:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 724.80 Td (Kafka follows a few simple rules:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 704.90 Td (If the producer does not provide a key, Kafka distributes records across partitions to balance load \(commonly) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 691.50 Td (round-robin or sticky partitioning depending on the client\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 671.60 Td (If the producer does provide a key, Kafka uses that key to consistently choose a partition.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 651.70 Td (Under the hood, this is usually:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 631.80 Td (Partition no = hash\(key\) % p, where p = number of partitions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 611.90 Td (Messages with the same key always go to the same partition, which means they are stored in order within that) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 598.50 Td (partition) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 578.60 Td (If we decide to change the number of partitions p later \(increase/decrease\), the same key may start routing to a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 565.20 Td (different partition, so there might not be ordering guarantee. \(so its always adviced to choose the partition) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 551.80 Td (number upfront based on the parallelism and throughput needs. \)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 531.90 Td (If needed, producers can also:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 512.00 Td (Directly specify the partition number, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 492.10 Td (Implement a custom partitioning logic \(useful, but should be done carefully to avoid hot partitions and uneven) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 478.70 Td (load\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 458.80 Td (I\222ll write a separate article in the coming weeks on the internals of the Kafka Producer. There\222s a lot happening) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 445.40 Td (behind the scenes when you call the Producer API, and understanding it makes it much easier to reason about) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 432.00 Td (scaling, idempotency, retries, and delivery guarantees.) Tj ET
